WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.756
Least privilege means the child process runs with only the permissions
needed for its approved purpose.

2
00:00:05.756 --> 00:00:11.316
It should not run as an administrator or root-equivalent account simply
because that is convenient.

3
00:00:11.316 --> 00:00:22.893
A background converter, report generator, build helper, or automation task
usually does not need broad filesystem access, broad network access, user
management permissions, or access to unrelated secrets.

4
00:00:22.893 --> 00:00:28.060
The execution identity should match the operation, not the most powerful
account available.

5
00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.592
Isolation can reduce damage if a process behaves unexpectedly.

6
00:00:31.592 --> 00:00:43.104
At a high level, isolation may involve service accounts, workload
identity, containers, sandboxing, read-only filesystems, restricted
volumes, limited network access, or separate worker environments.

7
00:00:43.104 --> 00:00:49.972
These controls vary by platform, but the goal is durable: limit what the
child process can see, change, contact, and persist.

8
00:00:49.972 --> 00:00:54.746
Isolation should be reviewed along with the application code that starts
the process.

9
00:00:54.746 --> 00:00:57.101
Resource controls protect availability.

10
00:00:57.101 --> 00:01:08.874
A child process that runs forever, produces unlimited output, opens too
many files, consumes too much CPU or memory, or starts too many concurrent
jobs can affect the parent application and shared infrastructure.

11
00:01:08.874 --> 00:01:17.312
Timeouts, output size limits, concurrency controls, queue limits,
cancellation behavior, and process termination rules should be part of the
design.

12
00:01:17.312 --> 00:01:22.675
Reliability settings are security-relevant when they prevent denial-of-
service conditions.

13
00:01:22.675 --> 00:01:25.226
Termination and cleanup need clear behavior.

14
00:01:25.226 --> 00:01:36.084
If a process times out, the application should know whether child work
stopped, whether temporary files remain, whether partial output is safe to
discard, and whether the operation can be retried.

15
00:01:36.084 --> 00:01:42.952
If the process is connected to a business transaction, the application
should avoid treating ambiguous failure as success.

16
00:01:42.952 --> 00:01:46.680
Safe execution controls not only what starts, but also how it stops.
